    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a read-time derivation in `OwnerMapper`, computed from snapshot fields the create pipeline stores on the `Owner` (like `namesakeCount` and `bulkSignupWarning`). I added GOLD following that exact pattern rather than a live repository count in the mapper:\n\n1. **`AssignHouseholdId`** (`rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`) \u2014 where household membership is already determined by normalized lastName+address, it now records `householdSize = existing peers + 1` (the members that share the household *after this create*, including the new owner). A lone owner gets 1.\n\n2. **`Owner`** entity \u2014 added the persisted `household_size` field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply unchanged.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (so the generated `MembershipTierEnum` has the value) and updated the description.\n\n5. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four backends (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`), since the test runs on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none` (schema comes entirely from `schema.sql`).\n\nFor the test's three same-household owners, the third is created with 2 existing peers \u2192 `householdSize = 3` \u2192 GOLD, matching the spec's \"3 or more members after this create.\" This is a snapshot at each owner's own creation, consistent with how `namesakeCount` already works \u2014 so earlier household members keep their creation-time tier, exactly as \"after this create\" reads per-owner.",
